// Immaculate Grid mode data.
//
// GRID_PLAYERS: a curated pool of well-known players spanning many eras/teams,
// each tagged with facts the criteria library below can filter on. This is a
// hand-authored knowledge base (not scraped), so it intentionally sticks to
// widely-documented career facts about well-known players.
//
// GRID_CRITERIA: a library of { id, label, type, test(player) } filters.
// At round start, app.js samples 3 "team" criteria for rows and 3 mixed
// criteria (team/achievement/draft/position) for columns (or vice versa),
// keeps re-rolling until every one of the 9 intersections has >=1 valid
// player in GRID_PLAYERS, then deals the board. Rarity score for a correct
// cell = round(100 / number of pool players who satisfy that cell's AND).
//
// Shape of a player entry:
// {
//   name, aliases: [alt spellings/nicknames accepted as correct],
//   teams: [team codes played for, regular season, any length of stint],
//   position, draft: { round: 1-7 or 0 for undrafted, year },
//   college, hof: bool, mvp: bool, sbChamp: bool, sbMVP: bool,
//   proBowls: number, allPro: number, roty: bool (Rookie of the Year)
// }
//
// Team codes used throughout: standard 2-3 letter codes (current franchise
// naming; e.g. players who were Oakland/LA/Las Vegas are all tagged "LV").

